# %% [md] 01 -- the space and the coefficients
# $\Gamma=\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ acts on the upper half plane $\mathfrak{H}$. The quotient $\Gamma\backslash\mathfrak{H}$ is an orbifold: a
# disc with two cone points, where the stabilisers are $\mathbb{Z}/4$ (at $i$) and $\mathbb{Z}/6$ (at $e^{2\pi i/3}$); the element $-1$
# acts trivially. HACS works with a finite triangulation of this quotient together with its isotropy groups.
#
# > **Coefficients.** For a prime $\ell$ and $n\ge0$ the coefficient system is the representation
# > $$V_n = \mathrm{Sym}^n\,\mathbb{F}_\ell^2,\qquad \dim V_n = n+1,$$
# > of $\Gamma$ (homogeneous polynomials of degree $n$ in two variables). Here $n=10$ and $\ell=691$, so $\dim V_{10}=11$.
#
# In the notebook every `display(...)` is rendered (TeX, tables); in a script it prints the canonical text.

# %% The model of SL_2(Z)\H
# The coefficient ring is the default F_ell, stated here so that the file runs in any order in one session (08 sets Z).
set coefficient_ring = "F_ell";
M = sl2z_model();
display(M);
assert(M.vertices == 7 and M.dims == [7, 11, 5], "7 vertices, 11 edges, 5 triangles");

# %% The coefficients Sym^10 over F_691
L = symmetric_power(M, 10, 691);
display(L);
assert(L.d_V == 11 and L.n + 1 == L.d_V, "dim Sym^10 = 11");

# %% [md] Reading the output
# | Mathematics | What HACS computed, and how |
# |---|---|
# | A triangulation of $\Gamma\backslash\mathfrak{H}$ (compactified by a boundary circle: a disc, Euler characteristic 1), and the two
#   finite stabilisers $\mathbb{Z}/4$, $\mathbb{Z}/6$. |
#   `sl2z_model()`: the 7-vertex model `sl2z_7vertex` (7 vertices, 11 edges, 5 triangles), with its exact tessellation tables.
#   Everything later is computed from this finite object. |
# | The local system $V_{10}=\mathrm{Sym}^{10}\mathbb{F}_{691}^2$ on the orbifold. |
#   `symmetric_power(M, 10, 691)`: a `LocalSystem` with `d_V = 11` (the rank) and its monodromy relations along the edges. |
